<title>SWEDEN: Swedish Riksbank board meeting ends, no changes.</title>
<headline>Swedish Riksbank board meeting ends, no changes.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The board of Sweden's central bank, the Riksbank, ended a meeting with no changes to interest rates announced.</p>
<p>Market players had not expected the bank to make any changes.</p>
<p>The Riksbank has not changed its key interest rate, the repo rate, since December 17 when it was lowered to its current level of 4.10 percent.</p>
<p>Its other key rates, the deposit and lending rates, currently stand at 3.75 percent and 5.25 percent respectively.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1045</p>
